WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.769
Every cloud has its own
certificate service,

2
00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:06.150
and each one can issue and
renew certificates by itself.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.437
Azure has Key Vault, AWS has Certificate
Manager, and Google has its own.

4
00:00:11.437 --> 00:00:14.413
Nobody coordinates them
unless the program does.

5
00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:20.425
So the rule is: for each certificate, decide
one renewer, and record it in the CLM.

6
00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:24.094
Either the CLM issues it and
pushes it into the cloud,

7
00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:27.337
or the cloud issues it
and the CLM just watches.

8
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:28.775
And notice the red band.

9
00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:30.975
Keys and secrets are a different job.

10
00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:34.500
They stay with each cloud's
own key and secret services.

11
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.800
The CLM manages certificates, not secrets.
